# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/drafter-bf16 four-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/drafter-bf16 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dbf16-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/drafter-bf16 commit; a commit of a file the image carries needs a new
# E4: EIGHT-SEAT timed arm B of the paired ABAB (131k windows, audits off): the bf16 drafter; A = c2-packed-tp4-8-best-quad, B = c2-packed-tp4-8-best-quad-dbf16; the pair differs in QWEN_FAST_DRAFTER_BF16 alone.
# The eight-seat round runs TWO 64-row quad drafts (about 1.9 ms of extra weight read at bf16 against a ~299 ms round, 0.65%): the number that bears on the 8-seat target. Arms alternate A B A B in this one
# image, each after its own all-four reset, same admission order. Runs only if S1 passed (NEEDS in ORDER.txt). An attach refusal on a B arm (the bf16 weights add about 405 MB per chip) is a FINDING recorded
# against the 131k eight-seat fit, not a window failure. NOT the 8x262k pool (see docs/tp4-drafter-bf16.md for that twin's block count).
# READ: after all four arms, offline: py -3.11 -B scripts/ci/drafter_bf16.py compare <A server log> <B server log> --live 8 (rounds paired by episode and index; at eight seats the '[PHASE] execute' step carries both
# blocks, so a round is the whole eight-user step), and scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py <A results> <B results> --users 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 --position-keyed --strict-concurrent-prefixes (texts identical). Judge PAIRED per round.
# Duration (estimate): 60 min.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-dbf16-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8-best-quad-dbf16
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_steady
